workflows[2].sections.splice(1,0,['browser','Try the complete calculation in your browser',`<p>The <a href="../tools/weekly-sales-reconciler.html">weekly sales reconciler</a> calculates the same example locally. Load the fictional sample, inspect the date window and day-first convention, and run the report. The sample enables removal of the one known exact repeated record.</p><figure class="figure"><img src="../assets/sales-reconciler-example.png" alt="Actual browser output showing 14 source records reconciled to RM267.60 net sales and the four product totals." width="1066" height="570" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Actual output from the built-in fictional sample. Source counts, net sales, and SKU totals match the worked workbook.</figcaption></figure><p>Each source record has a decision and a reason. The counts must reconcile: 14 source records = nine included + one repeated record removed + two outside the dates + two with other statuses. Invalid amounts, unresolved dates, and conflicting line keys keep the total unavailable until reviewed.</p><p>For a deliberate counterexample, turn exact-repeat removal off. The sample's total becomes RM315.60 because the repeated RM48.00 line remains. This is a preview of the consequence, not a recommendation to delete repeated rows in an unfamiliar source.</p>`]);
for(const w of workflows)w.time=Math.max(2,Math.ceil(w.sections.map(s=>s[2]).join(' ').replace(/<[^>]*>/g,' ').split(/\s+/).length/190));
